---
// The fee terms here are the ones the claim panel and the featured dialog
// already state on the county page. If those change, this has to change with
// them, or the site is promising two different things in two places.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const UPDATED = 'September 10, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use | Verified Home Inspector"
  description="The terms for using Verified Home Inspector, including what a listing is, how featured placements are paid, and what the site does and does not guarantee."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="legal">
        <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>

        <p>
          Verified Home Inspector is operated by Sunstate Bay Ventures LLC, a Florida limited
          liability company. Using the site means accepting what follows. If you do not accept
          it, please do not use the site.
        </p>

        <h2>What this directory is</h2>
        <p>
          It is a list of home inspectors licensed by the Florida Department of Business and
          Professional Regulation, built from the license records that agency publishes. Being
          listed is not a recommendation, an endorsement, or a statement that an inspector is
          any good. It means the DBPR record showed an active license when the data was last
          imported.
        </p>
        <p>
          Verify a license yourself with the DBPR before hiring anyone. Records change between
          imports, and the state's own lookup is the authoritative source, not this site.
        </p>

        <h2>We are not a party to your inspection</h2>
        <p>
          Passing your request to an inspector does not make us part of whatever you agree with
          them. The price, the scope, the schedule, the report, and any dispute about the work
          are between you and the inspector. We do not supervise inspections, we do not review
          reports, and we are not responsible for the work performed.
        </p>

        <h2>Nothing here is professional advice</h2>
        <p>
          The questions and answers on this site describe how inspections and Florida insurance
          requirements generally work, including references to Florida statutes. That is general
          information, not legal, insurance, engineering, or financial advice, and it is not a
          substitute for advice about your own house from someone you have hired. Statutes and
          carrier requirements change. Confirm anything that matters with your agent, your
          attorney, or the relevant agency before you rely on it.
        </p>

        <h2>Paid placements</h2>
        <p>
          Featured spots at the top of a county page are paid. They are labeled as paid
          placements wherever they appear, and paying for one changes only where a listing sits
          on the page. It does not change how a license is verified, and it never causes an
          unpaid inspector to be removed or hidden. Every licensed inspector in a covered county
          is listed whether they pay or not.
        </p>

        <h2>Claiming a listing</h2>
        <p>
          Claim a listing only if you hold that license or are authorized by the person who does.
          Claiming one you have no right to is a misrepresentation and we will remove it. We
          verify a claim against the DBPR record before a listing goes live.
        </p>
        <p>
          A claimed listing is free until we have passed it five homeowner requests. After that
          it is $10 a month, or $50 a month for a featured spot. Inspectors who take a featured
          spot early keep that rate for as long as they stay on it. Nothing is charged until a
          listing is live and the inspector has seen it, and requests are passed to one inspector
          at a time — we do not charge per lead and we do not send the same homeowner to several
          people.
        </p>

        <h2>Accuracy</h2>
        <p>
          The directory is only as current as the last DBPR import. A license may have been
          renewed, suspended, or surrendered since. If you find a listing that is wrong, tell us
          and we will correct it against the current record.
        </p>

        <h2>Things you may not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Scrape, harvest, or bulk-copy the directory, whether by script or by hand.</li>
          <li>Submit a request you do not intend, or submit forms automatically.</li>
          <li>Claim a listing you have no right to, or misrepresent who you are.</li>
          <li>Interfere with the site or try to reach parts of it that are not public.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The underlying license data is public record and you are free to get it from the DBPR
          yourself. The arrangement, writing, and design of this site are ours.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The site is provided as it is. We do not warrant that it will be uninterrupted, that
          every listing is accurate at the moment you read it, or that an inspector you contact
          will respond or will be available.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent Florida law allows it, Sunstate Bay Ventures LLC is not liable for
          indirect or consequential losses arising from use of the site, from anything a listing
          said, or from work an inspector performed. Nothing here limits any liability that
          cannot be limited by law.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Florida, and any dispute belongs
          in the state or federal courts serving Pinellas County, Florida.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If these terms change, the date at the top of the page changes with them. Continuing to
          use the site after that means accepting the revised terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions go through the same forms as everything else. Use the
          <a href="/fl/pinellas/#claim">form on the directory page</a> and we will reply to the
          address you give us.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
